    "text": {
      "en": "Stands on a 40 m tower on the Albis ridge southwest of Zurich, above the Sihl valley. It watches the whole of northern Switzerland. Its current dual-polarisation radar replaced a 1994 system in 2012, adding nine decibels of sensitivity partly by moving the transmitter to the top of the tower."
