      "en": "Stands at 2850 m on the Weissfluhgipfel between Davos and Arosa in Graubünden, reached by cable car. It covers the eastern Swiss Alps, where valleys used to sit in the shadow of other radars. Construction began in May 2014 and it went into service in January 2016 as the fifth Swiss radar."
